[- Concept: Data Model. -]
[page id='data-model'
  [meta
    title='Data Model (CXDM)'
    layout='concept'
    nav-order='200'
    audience='learner'
    summary='One tree shape under every dialect. Elements, attributes, body items, structural slots.'
  ]

  [section id='overview' title='One Tree, Six Surfaces'
    [prose CXDM is the shape every CX parse produces and every emit walks. Whether the source is CX, XML, JSON, YAML, TOML, or Markdown, the parser yields a tree in this single shape; whether the target is any of those six dialects, the emitter walks the same tree back out. Downstream code never branches on input format because the data model has already absorbed the difference.]
  ]

  [section id='element' title='The Element'
    [prose A CXDM node is an Element with a name, an ordered list of attributes, an ordered list of body items, and a few optional structural slots — anchor, merge target, declared id, data type. Body items are Text nodes, Scalar nodes, child Elements, or the collection literals from ADR 0017 — Sequences, Arrays, Maps.]
    [code lang='cx' src='''[pizza #margherita :large size=14 crust=thin
  [topping cheese]
  [topping basil]
  Stone-baked since 1987.]''']
    [prose Reading this element from the outside in: name pizza, declared id margherita, data-type annotation :large, attributes size=14 and crust=thin, then a body of three items — two child elements and a text node.]
  ]

  [section id='attrs' title='Attributes'
    [prose Attributes are name=value pairs after the element name. Values can be bare, single-quoted, double-quoted, or triple-quoted. Bare values are auto-typed: 8080 becomes int, 3.14 becomes float, true becomes bool, 2026-01-01 becomes date. Leading-zero tokens stay strings — 02134 stays the string 02134 — to avoid the YAML Norway problem.]
  ]

  [section id='body' title='Body Items in Order'
    [prose A body holds Text, Scalar, child Element, or collection literal in source order. Mixed content is first-class: text and structure can interleave the way they do in XML and Markdown, the way JSON cannot.]
    [code lang='cx' src='[note Try the [b Margherita] — our [em best seller], hand-tossed daily.]']
  ]

  [section id='collections' title='Collection Literals'
    [prose ADR 0017 brings three collection shapes as first-class body and attribute values. Sequence with parens flattens; array with brackets preserves nesting; map with braces gives named key-to-value entries.]
    [code lang='cx' src='''[pizza toppings=(cheese, basil, oil)]
[grid cells=[[1,0,1],[0,1,0],[1,0,1]]]
[pizza prices={small: 9, medium: 12, large: 15}]''']
  ]

  [section id='structural-slots' title='Structural Slots'
    [prose Beyond name, attributes, and body, an element carries optional structural slots. Each slot is signalled by a sigil; each carries a single value or reference.]
    [list
      [item path='concepts/sigils' label='Anchor (ampersand) — names this element so others can refer to or merge from it']
      [item path='concepts/sigils' label='Merge target (asterisk) — copies attributes and children from a named anchor']
      [item path='concepts/identity' label='Declared id (hash) — stable identifier within scope; targets of references']
      [item path='concepts/types'   label='Data type (colon) — pins the body or value type, overriding auto-typing']
    ]
  ]

  [section id='whitespace' title='Whitespace Significance'
    [prose Whitespace inside a body is significant when it sits between text characters and collapses to a single space when it separates body items. The canonical form normalises this so byte-identical content carries the same hash regardless of source author choice.]
  ]

  [section id='related' title='Related'
    [list
      [item path='concepts/sigils'      label='Sigils & Markup']
      [item path='concepts/identity'    label='Identity & Canonical Form']
      [item path='concepts/types'       label='Types']
      [item path='reference/grammar'    label='Grammar (EBNF)']
    ]
  ]

  [preserve id='author-notes'
    [- Empty by default. -]
  ]
]
